# Day 22: Spring Boot DevTools - Stop Restarting!

Today I learned how to speed up my development workflow using **Spring Boot DevTools**.

### ⚡ The "Automatic Restart" Feature
Normally, every time you change a single line of Java code, you have to stop the app and click "Run" again. DevTools fixes this:
* Whenever you save a file, DevTools detects the change and **restarts the application automatically** in the background.
* It uses a "smart restart" strategy that only reloads your code (not the entire library stack), making it 10x faster than a full manual restart.

### 🌐 LiveReload
DevTools includes an embedded **LiveReload server**. If you are building a web interface (using Thymeleaf or HTML), the browser will automatically refresh the page the moment you save your code. No more hitting `F5`!

### 🛠️ How to enable it:
Just add this one dependency to your `pom.xml`:
```xml
<dependency>
    <groupId>org.springframework.boot</groupId>
    <artifactId>spring-boot-devtools</artifactId>
    <optional>true</optional>
</dependency>
